  - Name: monster1104_name
    Text: Obsidian Stalker
  - Name: monster0_des
    Text: Freshly hatched from its ancient egg, Wyrmote is a mischievous young drake
      still half-shelled but full of spirit. Though its said this Echo pulses with
      dormant elemental energy, and carries the legacy of an extinct dragonblood
      line, Wyrmote bonds quickly with Scions who show courage-and has a curious
      habit of waddling into danger without hesitation.
  - Name: monster1_des
    Text: "A twisted result of forbidden alchemy and forgotten tech, Twynthrax is
      the evolved form of Wyrmote-its innocence long shattered. Now a dual-headed
      terror, part bone and part machine, it roams with eerie precision and a hunger
      for control. Each head holds a mind of its own: one driven by instinct, the
      other by cold calculation. Though fearsome in battle, echoes of its former
      self flicker in rare moments of hesitation\u2026 as if the hatchling within
      still remembers."
  - Name: monster2_des
    Text: "Triphyrex towers as a tri-headed abomination forged from bone, flesh,
      and relentless steel. Each head speaks a different truth: wrath, wisdom, and
      will-never in agreement, yet always united in destruction. Once a fragile hatchling,
      it has become a living war engine, powered by corrupted elemental cores and
      ancient tech long thought lost. Legends say only a Scion of great resolve can
      control its fury\u2026 or survive its betrayal."
  - Name: monster3_des
    Text: Once an ordinary woodland cub, Bruisic was taken by rogue alchemists experimenting
      with volatile elemental serums. The injection left a strange green glow pulsing
      through its veins, unlocking a ferocity far beyond its small frame. Though
      it still bears the instincts of a curious cub, Bruisic now lashes out with
      bursts of unnatural strength-caught between the beast it was and the monster
      it may become.
  - Name: monster4_des
    Text: The mutation deepens as Bruisic evolves into Bradiate-a terrifying fusion
      of raw muscle, exposed bone, and toxic rage. Fueled by twin canisters of unstable
      serum, Bradiate's body now leaks green energy that scorches the ground with
      every step. Its roar spreads panic, and its strikes leave a corrosive mark.
      Whatever innocence the cub once had is buried beneath layers of pain, leaving
      only a relentless predator shaped by alchemy and agony.
  - Name: monster5_des
    Text: The ultimate result of unchecked experimentation, Brutoxar is a monstrous
      juggernaut of metal, toxin, and fury. A reinforced horn crowns its armored
      skull, while serrated steel fangs tear through anything in its path. The canister
      on its back pumps an endless supply of volatile serum into its bloodstream,
      keeping it in a constant state of berserk mutation. Brutoxar no longer feels
      fear-or pain. It exists only to rampage, a living weapon whose rage can barely
      be contained.
  - Name: monster6_des
    Text: Don't let the name fool you-Fluffalo is all grit wrapped in fur. Born in
      the storm-forged highlands, this stout horned warrior trains from a young age
      in brutal rites of strength and endurance. With fists like boulders and a heart
      twice the size, Fluffalo charges headfirst into any challenge, always eager
      to prove that even the smallest fighter can shake the ground. Loyal, headstrong,
      and surprisingly tactical, Fluffalo is a steadfast companion to any Scion brave
      enough to earn his respect.
  - Name: monster7_des
    Text: Forged through battle and hardened by fire, Blazuff is the evolved embodiment
      of Fluffalo's indomitable will. His frame now towers with muscle, his armor
      etched with tribal symbols of triumph, and a flame blazes at the tip of his
      tail-burning brighter with his rising fury. No longer just a determined scrapper,
      Blaszuff leads with honor, striking with the force of an avalanche and the
      precision of a seasoned warrior. When he fights, it's not just for victory-but
      for legacy.
  - Name: monster8_des
    Text: A living inferno clad in battle-forged armor, Pyronax is the apex of Fluffalo's
      fiery lineage. His mane blazes like a wildfire, and every movement leaves trails
      of smoldering embers in his wake. Fueled by rage and resolve, Pyronax wields
      molten strength capable of leveling even the toughest foes. His presence alone
      ignites the battlefield-both in flame and in courage. To stand beside him is
      to march with the fury of a volcano at your side.
  - Name: monster9_des
    Text: Skittering beneath the surface of dry, cracked earth, Cragmite is a small
      but heavily-armored Echo known for ambushing from below. Its jagged carapace
      blends seamlessly with rocky terrain, while its piercing legs can burrow through
      stone with ease. Despite its size, it's feared by miners and scavengers alike-its
      bite can destabilize ground formations in seconds. Watch your step, for where
      the land trembles, a Cragmite may be lurking.
  - Name: monster10_des
    Text: Tharnok is the monstrous evolution of Cragmite-no longer a lurking crawler,
      but a mobile fortress of stone and bone. Its six razor-edged legs pulverize
      terrain as it charges, while its massive maw bristles with jagged teeth ready
      to shred through steel. Spikes jut from its rock-hard carapace like warning
      signs carved by nature itself. Once a hidden threat, Tharnok now rules the
      battlefield as a relentless, earthborn predator feared even by seasoned Scions.
  - Name: monster11_des
    Text: Whispers speak of Bedrakul as an ancient terror buried since the First
      Collapse, a creature born of Gaia's wrath and sharpened by centuries beneath
      stone. Towering and unrelenting, it now rises with eight jagged limbs and two
      colossal bone scythes that rend earth and flesh alike. Its armored shell pulses
      with green fissures of dormant elemental energy, and its presence alone can
      cause tremors in the land. Bedrakul does not hunt-it cleanses, leaving nothing
      behind but dust and silence. To face it is to challenge the will of the earth
      itself.
  - Name: monster12_des
    Text: "A race from the coastal ruins of a long-flooded civilization, Ripmaw is
      a fierce and agile predator that stalks tidal flats and shipwrecks alike. Wielding
      a rusted hook torn from a sunken trawler, he fights with a mix of raw instinct
      and calculated strikes. His icy blue fur crackles with condensed moisture,
      and his roar echoes like a crashing wave. Though still young, Ripmaw is relentless\u2014and
      his fury builds with every battle won beneath the waves."
  - Name: monster13_des
    Text: "No longer just a scavenger of the ruins, Brinefang has become a warbringer
      of the floodlands. His crude hook has been reforged into a serrated blade of
      shipwreck steel, and arcs of water-charged energy now crackle along his armored
      form. Infused with the power of tidal stones lost to the deep, Brinefang moves
      with both feral precision and brutal purpose. His howl carries the weight of
      crashing waves\u2014and when it rises, even the tide itself seems to recoil."
  - Name: monster14_des
    Text: "From the shattered tides of forgotten coasts rises Nautherak, the apex
      form of Ripmaw's evolution and a warlord of the storm-swept deeps. Clad in
      abyss-forged armor and wielding a cruel tidehook charged with the fury of the
      sea, Nautherak surges with crackling energy\u2014his body constantly arcing
      with volatile currents. Each strike sends tremors through the battlefield,
      and his presence alone twists the air with pressure and static. No longer just
      a beast of instinct, Nautherak is a living legend\u2014whispered in sailor's
      prayers and feared in Scion war songs."
  - Name: monster15_des
    Text: "Varnok is a territorial juggernaut of the jungle\u2014part beast, part
      blooming terror. Its thick limbs are rooted in ancient growth, covered in bark-like
      plating and hardened by centuries of survival in the darkest canopies. Once
      whispered of in tribal legend, it now strikes with terrifying speed, wings
      flared and eyes burning with primal instinct. Its razor-sharp claws tear through
      undergrowth and armor alike, clearing all who trespass in its domain. Varnok
      does not hunt for food\u2014it hunts to dominate."
  - Name: monster16_des
    Text: "Varnokar is no longer just a jungle predator\u2014it is a sovereign force
      of nature. Adorned with bark-forged armor and ritual markings carved by those
      who revere or fear it, Varnokar commands its territory with calculated ferocity.
      Its wings now serve more for intimidation than flight, and its razor claws
      strike like scythes through stone and steel. Every movement carries the weight
      of a creature that has survived\u2014and dominated\u2014the wild for generations.
      In the heart of the jungle, Varnokar is law."
  - Name: monster17_des
    Text: "Varnokarnyx is no longer a beast, but a legend of Gaia's wild heart\u2014armored
      in gilded barkstone and crowned with relics of forgotten ages. Every movement
      gleams with ceremonial power, its claws now monstrous scythes bound in ritual
      steel. Adorned in sacred plating and thrumming with elemental presence, Varnokarnyx
      does not stalk the jungle\u2014it rules it. Few dare enter its domain, and
      none leave unchanged. When Varnokarnyx rises, even the jungle holds its breath."
  - Name: monster18_des
    Text: "Bruntide is a coastal enforcer forged by tide and trial. With thick, scale-plated
      skin and the strength to weather crashing waves, he's often found guarding
      ancient sea routes and sunken ruins. His axe, shaped from bone and reefstone,
      delivers slow but crushing blows that leave deep impressions\u2014both in enemies
      and the land they tread. Though not quick to anger, when Bruntide moves to
      strike, it's with the weight of the ocean behind him."
  - Name: monster19_des
    Text: "Brutusk has emerged from countless coastal skirmishes as a seasoned predator
      of the sea. His once-simple shell has hardened into a near-impenetrable fortress,
      while his thickened hide now turns blades and arrows alike. Adorned in the
      bones of fallen foes and wielding a brutal, hooked axe, Brutusk fights not
      just to win\u2014but to make sure no one dares return. Every step he takes
      echoes like thunder against stone, and in his presence, even armored Scions
      learn fear. The ocean is no longer just his home\u2014it's his territory."
  - Name: monster20_des
    Text: "Brutalmar is not merely an Echo\u2014he is an event. A war titan of the
      sea, encased in bone-wrought armor and crowned with the remnants of every challenger
      he's crushed. His hulking frame moves with the inevitability of a rising tide,
      each step quaking the earth beneath. His shell, now denser than the strongest
      forged steel, shrugs off blades, spells, and siege alike. With legs like stone
      pillars and an axe that ends battles with a single swing,  Brutalmar is a siege
      engine made flesh. His enemies don't flee\u2014they crumble. The ocean follows
      him not as an ally, but as a weapon unleashed."
  - Name: monster21_des
    Text: "Built in the final throes of a crumbling empire, this armored Echo was
      forged in secret beneath the molten furnaces of Gaia's deepest forges. Known
      only by code and purpose, it was engineered to be the perfect foot soldier\u2014unyielding,
      tireless, and devoid of mercy. But when the Astral Gate fell and the empire
      vanished in the Collapse, so too did the chains of control. Now, it roams the
      broken lands of Gaia, a living engine of war twisted by centuries of corrupted
      elemental energy."
  - Name: monster22_des
    Text: "The war machine once known as Strathex has not remained idle. After centuries
      of wandering Gaia's scarred surface, it absorbed fragments of forgotten alloys,
      corrupted crystals, and astral debris left behind after the Collapse. Drawn
      to ruptures of the ancient Astral Gates, his core began to mutate\u2014not
      decay, but evolve. The molten veins of Gaia fused his systems with unstable
      elemental energy, triggering a volatile rebirth. Now reforged as Strathexen,
      his alloyed frame crackles with raw power, no longer a mindless relic\u2014but
      a vengeance-driven juggernaut, fueled not by command, but by rage."
  - Name: monster23_des
    Text: "What began as Strathex, a discarded weapon of war, has become something
      far more terrifying. After his volatile rebirth into Strathexen, the entity
      once bound by programming has fully awakened. Seeking out the buried remnants
      of Gaia's oldest forges and sites of pre-Collapse experimentation, he unearthed
      alloyed relics infused with pure elemental cores\u2014long sealed away by the
      Astral Alliance. As his corrupted systems integrated these forbidden materials,
      a final transformation began. No longer merely remembering rage, Strathexar
      embodies it. He is not a weapon. He is a reckoning\u2014forged from the ruins,
      empowered by the Collapse, and driven by a will no master can command."
  - Name: monster24_des
    Text: Forged from the ashes of a silent eruption, this fiery beast is the first
      flame of Braizoal's rebirth. With each step, scorched earth smolders beneath
      his claws. He hunts through Gaia's volcanic scars, guided by fury and memory.
      Though his form is young, the fire within burns forever remembering the night
      the mountains betrayed him.
  - Name: monster25_des
    Text: The fire no longer trails behind, but erupts from within. After countless
      battles across Gaia's smoldering wounds, Braiz has evolved into a living conduit
      of molten fury. His hide, now armored in volcanic plates, crackles with heat,
      and his breath scorches air before it's spoken. Flames dance in his mane, tail,
      and across his path. This is no longer the fire that remembers. This is the
      fire that acts.
  - Name: monster26_des
    Text: There is no ash left to grieve, but only vengeance that walks. Braizoal's
      final form is a blazing revenant of fury and resolve. His bone-forged tail
      and scorched skull burn with ancestral flame, hotter than magma, brighter than
      the first eruption. No longer seeking revenge for he is the reckoning. Wherever
      he runs, volcanoes tremble, for their time of judgment has come.
  - Name: monster27_des
    Text: "No longer cloaked in shadow, Hylja has taken a new form.  With her lower
      body now entwined with the forest beast she once imitated, and her staff brimming
      with elemental wisdom, she defends sacred glades from corruption. Her raven
      guides lost souls, and punishes those who stray with impure intent. Some Scions
      report her warning gaze\u2026 others remember only the trees closing in."
  - Name: monster28_des
    Text: No longer just a forest illusion, Hyldr has embraced her purpose as a guardian
      of balance. With her gemstaff pulsing with ancient verdant power, and her raven
      ever at her side, she weaves protective wards and vengeful curses in equal
      measure. Those who dare disturb Gaia's harmony find their strength sapped by
      vines unseen, and their path lost in eternal mist.
  - Name: monster29_des
    Text: Now fully awakened as the forest's sovereign, Huldra channels the raw will
      of Gaia itself. Her staff's emerald heart glows with ancestral memory, and
      her voice carries command over leaf, beast, and shadow. The raven perched by
      her side is no longer a scout, but a herald of reckoning. In Huldra's domain,
      nature does not forgive. It remembers. And it reclaims.
  - Name: monster2000_des
    Text: Born from the ashes of forgotten battlegrounds, Smokage is a swift and
      silent flame wreathed in shadow. Cloaked in scorched garb and wielding a searing
      blade, this elusive figure darts through the battlefield like smoke in the
      wind. Embers trail behind every motion, and his burning gaze pierces through
      darkness with unwavering focus. Scions whisper that he is the remnant of a
      fallen warrior spirit, cursed to fight in eternal silence-striking fast, vanishing
      faster.
  - Name: monster2001_des
    Text: A hulking brute shaped from molten alloy and ancient circuitry, Gholyx
      lumbers through the ruins of forgotten forges. Its single, unblinking eye glows
      with silent purpose, scanning for intruders and lost relics. Encased in scorched
      orange-metal armor, its chest bears a circular core believed to regulate its
      internal pressure and power. With arms heavy as anvils and legs built purely
      for stability, Gholyx strikes like a collapsing pillar-slow, deliberate, and
      devastating.
  - Name: monster2002_des
    Text: Slow, silent, and endlessly enduring, Tarsok is a deep-sea wanderer risen
      from the ocean floor. Its thick, spiral shell is encrusted with jagged coral,
      remnants of a lifetime spent drifting through reef graveyards and underwater
      trenches. Though its movements are glacial, each step carries the weight of
      centuries. With a single glowing eye and a body that pulses with tidal energy,
      Tarsok embodies the patience and crushing power of the sea itself-unstoppable
      when provoked.
  - Name: monster2003_des
    Text: A mysterious being of grace and menace, Raviel stands tall like a shadow-forged
      steed, wings folded in silent defiance. Though his form appears elegant, his
      true strength lies beneath-bones forged from metal-rich essence, unyielding
      to blade or flame. With eyes like molten gold and horns that hum with elemental
      resonance, Raviel glides through the battlefield with haunting poise. Few dare
      to confront him head-on, for every step he takes echoes like armor across the
      plains of war.
  - Name: monster2004_des
    Text: A swift and merciless predator of the wild skies, Venomelra darts through
      the air in flashes of violet and gold. With translucent yellow wings and a
      venom-tipped stinger that glows like molten amber, this wasp-like Echo is as
      beautiful as it is deadly. Its sleek form conceals powerful toxins brewed from
      rare flora, making even a single sting potentially paralyzing. Few see it coming-fewer
      still live to tell the tale.
  - Name: monster2005_des
    Text: A rare marvel of the skies and seas, Caelivra drifts through the air with
      serene grace, its icy-blue and white wings glistening like waves beneath moonlight.
      Though born of the Water element, it rarely touches the ground-preferring to
      hover on ocean winds and misty currents. Its singular eye radiates calm intelligence,
      while its luminous antenna senses shifts in weather and tides. Gentle in nature
      but elusive, Caelivra is often mistaken for a spirit of the storm.
  - Name: monster2006_des
    Text: Spawned from the festering shadows of corrupted ley lines, Dregmire is
      a malformed specter of elemental chaos. Its lone, unblinking eye burns with
      unnatural awareness, while green flames leak from its arms and head like toxic
      will made manifest. With gangly limbs and a body that seems to twitch between
      dimensions, Dregmire drifts across cursed zones, drawn to sites of decay and
      despair. Some Scions say it whispers-but no one who listened has ever remained
      the same.
  - Name: monster2007_des
    Text: Forged in the deepest veins of Gaia's crystal caverns, Obsilok is a sentinel
      of stone and shimmering rage. Its compact body is armored with jagged purple
      rock, while crimson crystals jut from its limbs like natural blades. A single
      glowing eye surveys its surroundings with cold, unwavering focus. Though silent
      and unmoving at rest, when the earth trembles, Obsilok awakens-striking with
      the fury of tectonic wrath to defend the balance beneath the surface.
  - Name: monster2008_des
    Text: Lurking among the dense undergrowth of Gaia's wildest regions, Oculorak
      is a grotesque fusion of plant and predator. Resembling a mutated Venus flytrap,
      its massive maw oozes corrosive sap and is lined with jagged, petal-like fangs
      ready to snap shut on anything that strays too close. Though rooted in the
      Nature element, Oculorak shows no gentleness-only hunger. Legends say its eye
      never blinks, always watching, waiting for the next careless step into its
      territory.
  - Name: monster2009_des
    Text: Burrowed deep within Gaia's shifting crust, Myrvok is a curious fusion
      of resilience and sensitivity. Its armored purple segments shield it from falling
      debris and predators, while its softer turquoise underbody allows it to wriggle
      through the narrowest crevices. A singular eye gleams beneath towering antennae,
      attuned to the tremors of the world around it. Though small, Myrvok is a vigilant
      guardian of the earth-emerging only when balance is disturbed beneath the surface.
  - Name: monster1000_des
    Text: "Zal'vhex is no mere commander\u2014he is a conduit. A prophet born of
      the Rift's deepest fracture, he channels raw void energy to destroy form, silence
      thought, and unravel resistance. Cloaked in ethereal fire and crowned with
      arcane symbols, Zal'vhex speaks a language that kills. His abilities bend time,
      space, and will, making him the apex threat of any Astral incursion."
  - Name: monster1001_des
    Text: "Ekzari is a matriarch of the Vraekir hive\u2014ancient, bloated, and revered.
      Her body is a breeding vat of bio-organic horrors, capable of spawning Swarmlings
      and mutagenic clouds mid-combat. Each of her children is psychically tethered
      to her will, and her hive consciousness can outmaneuver even the most disciplined
      strike teams. Her defeat does not mark an end\u2014it merely halts the tide.
      Unless sterilized, her spawn continue to gestate in the shadows of the battlefield."
  - Name: monster1002_des
    Text: "Xarnox is a mobile plague engine\u2014part scavenger, part shock trooper,
      all horror. Bulging with toxic growths and stitched together from harvested
      matter, its body mutates in real-time, adapting to damage and spewing filth
      across the battlefield. The Vraekir use harvesters like Xarnox to cleanse regions
      of resistance\u2014through digestion or decomposition. Its presence signals
      not just invasion, but infestation. Destroying it is not enough. You must also
      burn the earth it touched."
  - Name: monster1003_des
    Text: The Zynthari Warden is a psionic operative of the Vraekir swarm. Acting
      as both interrogator and executioner, it erodes its prey's mind before their
      body. The pulsating dome upon its skull acts as both amplifier and conduit
      for hive-borne psychic signals, letting it suppress enemy spells and cripple
      thoughts mid-battle. Once considered a myth among Rift Scholars, this creature's
      appearance at a gate signals the swarm's intent to escalate.
  - Name: monster1004_des
    Text: "The Obsidian Stalker is the Vraekir's first line of defense\u2014mass-produced,
      semi-sentient, and utterly relentless. Forged from obsidian chitin and pulse-reactive
      muscle fiber, this drone operates with a hive-bound efficiency that belies
      its simplicity. Though lesser among its kin, its speed and armor-shredding
      attacks make it a dangerous foe for the unprepared. These creatures are often
      encountered alone, scouting or guarding dormant gates, but once threatened,
      they become feral executioners."
  - Name: monster1100_des
    Text: "Zal'vhex is no mere commander\u2014he is a conduit. A prophet born of
      the Rift's deepest fracture, he channels raw void energy to destroy form, silence
      thought, and unravel resistance. Cloaked in ethereal fire and crowned with
      arcane symbols, Zal'vhex speaks a language that kills. His abilities bend time,
      space, and will, making him the apex threat of any Astral incursion."
  - Name: monster1101_des
    Text: "Ekzari is a matriarch of the Vraekir hive\u2014ancient, bloated, and revered.
      Her body is a breeding vat of bio-organic horrors, capable of spawning Swarmlings
      and mutagenic clouds mid-combat. Each of her children is psychically tethered
      to her will, and her hive consciousness can outmaneuver even the most disciplined
      strike teams. Her defeat does not mark an end\u2014it merely halts the tide.
      Unless sterilized, her spawn continue to gestate in the shadows of the battlefield."
  - Name: monster1102_des
    Text: "Xarnox is a mobile plague engine\u2014part scavenger, part shock trooper,
      all horror. Bulging with toxic growths and stitched together from harvested
      matter, its body mutates in real-time, adapting to damage and spewing filth
      across the battlefield. The Vraekir use harvesters like Xarnox to cleanse regions
      of resistance\u2014through digestion or decomposition. Its presence signals
      not just invasion, but infestation. Destroying it is not enough. You must also
      burn the earth it touched."
  - Name: monster1103_des
    Text: The Zynthari Warden is a psionic operative of the Vraekir swarm. Acting
      as both interrogator and executioner, it erodes its prey's mind before their
      body. The pulsating dome upon its skull acts as both amplifier and conduit
      for hive-borne psychic signals, letting it suppress enemy spells and cripple
      thoughts mid-battle. Once considered a myth among Rift Scholars, this creature's
      appearance at a gate signals the swarm's intent to escalate.
  - Name: monster1104_des
    Text: "The Obsidian Stalker is the Vraekir's first line of defense\u2014mass-produced,
      semi-sentient, and utterly relentless. Forged from obsidian chitin and pulse-reactive
      muscle fiber, this drone operates with a hive-bound efficiency that belies
      its simplicity. Though lesser among its kin, its speed and armor-shredding
      attacks make it a dangerous foe for the unprepared. These creatures are often
      encountered alone, scouting or guarding dormant gates, but once threatened,
      they become feral executioners."
