  - Name: clan_boss_rank
    Text: Rank
  - Name: clan_boss_rank_empty
    Text: None have dared to battle the Clan Boss. Will you be the first?
  - Name: clan_boss_total
    Text: '<color=blue>Total Fight</color> :  Your clan must complete a certain number
      of boss battles to receive the corresponding rewards based on the number of
      battles your clan has completed. The rewards will be sent to your mailbox the
      following day.'
  - Name: clan_boss_rewards
    Text: '<color=blue>Rewards </color> : For each damage milestone you reach, you''ll
      receive a reward box. Each box contains various rewards with different drop
      rates. The more damage you deal, the more rewards you''ll receive.'
  - Name: clan_boss_Key
    Text: '<color=blue>Keys </color> : Used to unlock boss battles. Each day, you
      will receive a certain number of keys.When you run out, you can earn more by
      watching ads to receive rewards.'
  - Name: summon_info_text
    Text: '*** You can only summon a monster that you haven''t unlocked yet. If you
      unlock a monster you already own, it will be converted into 100 shards. Shards
      can be used to upgrade that monster!***'
  - Name: arena_Point
    Text: Arena Point
  - Name: power_txt
    Text: Power
  - Name: defense_team
    Text: Defense Team
  - Name: battle_title
    Text: Battle
  - Name: result_title
    Text: Result
  - Name: leaderbord_title
    Text: LeaderBoard
  - Name: opponent_mess
    Text: You have already won this battle.Please choose another opponent.
  - Name: not_enough_arena_tickets
    Text: You need more Arena Tickets to start this battle.
  - Name: avatar
    Text: Avatar
  - Name: tut_0_1
    Text: "You have been awakened, Scion. Welcome back to Gaia.I am Myrk\u2026 not
      as I once was, but a vision, a whisper echoing across time.My purpose is to
      guide you\u2014to help you reclaim your strength and remember who you were\u2026
      and what you must become."
  - Name: tut_1_1
    Text: As an awakening gift, a message awaits you in your mail.Tap the mail icon
      to open your inbox and claim your reward.
  - Name: tut_1_2
    Text: Go ahead-open your message and claim your reward.You've taken your first
      steps, Scion. You'll need every advantage in the journey ahead.
  - Name: tut_2_1
    Text: This is the World Map of Gaia. Once a realm united by the Astral Gates,
      it now lies fractured and forgotten.Scattered across the land are Echoes-remnants
      of elemental beings once bonded with Scions like you.
  - Name: tut_2_2
    Text: "These Echoes are not mindless beasts. They were once allies, companions\u2026
      guardians.But the Great Collapse twisted the bond. Many now wander lost, consumed
      by elemental chaos.  Now you must fight, and collect their essence and then
      train them to fight by your side once more."
  - Name: tut_2_3
    Text: After you've chosen your battle on the world map you come to the pre-battle
      screen.  It will reveal what you are about to face, its elemental nature, and
      its power.  In this world, Scions battle through the strength of their Echoes. 
      Battles are automated and will continue till you win or lose.  Press Attack
      to continue.
  - Name: tut_2_4
    Text: "Press Attack when you are ready to face it.\u201D\u201CIn this world,
      Scions battle through the strength of their Echoes.Battles are automated and
      will continue till you win or lose."
  - Name: tut_3_1
    Text: Now, let us prepare you for the battles ahead.Tap the Heroes button at
      the bottom of your screen to view your gear and equipment.
  - Name: tut_3_2
    Text: 'This tome records all gear you''ve collected : armor, weapons, and relics
      of the old age.Equip your Scion to enhance the power of your Echo Companions.'
  - Name: tut_3_3
    Text: Tap on the shield to view its details.Here, you'll see the stats it grants
      your Scion and how it boosts your Echoes in battle.
  - Name: tut_3_4
    Text: "On this screen, you can upgrade this gear to enhance its effects\u2026or
      sell it if you no longer need it."
  - Name: tut_3_5
    Text: Each upgrade requires resources such as gear stones and coins.Invest wisely,
      Scion. The strength of your Echoes often begins with the armor you wear.
  - Name: tut_4_1
    Text: Tap on the Bag button at the bottom of your screen to open your backpack.
  - Name: tut_4_2
    Text: Here you'll find all the items you collect during your battles and adventures.From
      food, to keys, to precious Echo Shards. Everything is stored here.
  - Name: tut_4_3
    Text: Running low on space? You may expand your bag for a small fee in gems.Be
      prepared, Scion , even the smallest item may shape the fate of your journey.
  - Name: tut_5_1
    Text: "Press the \u201CLine Up\u201D button at the bottom of the screen."
  - Name: tut_5_2
    Text: This is your Echo Lineup screen.Here, you may add, remove, or reposition
      your Echoes to prepare for battle.A strategic line up is crucial and can turn
      the tide of any battle.
  - Name: tut_6_1
    Text: Your journey across Gaia is filled with purpose.Tap the Quest button below
      to see the trials laid before you.
  - Name: tut_6_2
    Text: Here you'll find quests to complete each day, as well as long-term challenges.Each
      task brings rewards such as gold, gems, and other resources that will aid you
      in your battles throughout Gaia.
  - Name: tut_7_1
    Text: Tap on the Monster button at the bottom of your screen.Here is where your
      Echo Companions await your guidance.
  - Name: tut_7_2
    Text: This is where you can view your Echoes.Select one to upgrade or evolve.
      Tap the Upgrade button to continue.
  - Name: tut_7_3
    Text: "This is the Echo's enhancement screen.You can choose to Level Up, Star
      Up, or even Evolve your Echo\u2014if you possess the right materials."
  - Name: tut_8_1
    Text: Tap on the Market button.
  - Name: tut_8_2
    Text: "Welcome to the Market, Scion.Here, you can purchase powerful accessories
      to help in battle\u2014or stylish gear to change your appearance."
  - Name: tut_8_3
    Text: You can also acquire gold and gems here,useful for everything from gear
      upgrades to evolving Echoes.
  - Name: tut_8_4
    Text: "Check back often.You never know when something rare\u2026 or a timely
      sale\u2026 might appear."
  - Name: tut_9_1
    Text: "I must bid you farewell, brave Scion.You now carry the knowledge needed
      to continue your training ,to rise again as a protector of Gaia.A Scion worthy
      of restoring what was lost\u2026 and defending what remains."
  - Name: tut_9_2
    Text: "Remember this: you are not alone.Many Scions across Gaia have awakened
      , ready to fight by your side\u2026 or call upon your aid in their time of
      need.The path ahead will challenge you, but it will also shape you.Go now,
      and let your legend begin."
  - Name: tut_10_1
    Text: Hello, Scion. I am Thalric Vorn-Arena Master. Warden of Valor. Keeper of
      the Echo Trials.I see you've grown strong enough to enter the Arena.
  - Name: tut_10_2
    Text: The Arena isn't just a place to test strength. It's where strategy meets
      might.Your Echoes-your choices-will face the fiercest contenders Gaia has to
      offer.But first... let's step inside.
  - Name: tut_10_3
    Text: Every week, warriors like you rise and fall. Points are earned. Glory is
      claimed.And rewards? Those go to the bold.
  - Name: tut_10_4
    Text: Now that you're here, let's set up your Defense Team.
  - Name: tut_10_5
    Text: Here, you'll assign which of your companions will defend and fight for
      your honor in the Arena.
  - Name: tut_10_6
    Text: Back on the main arena, you'll see your opponents.You can refresh the list
      every 15 minutes, or pay a small fee to do it early.
  - Name: tut_10_7
    Text: Curious about the ranks, rewards, and what it takes to climb
  - Name: tut_10_8
    Text: And if you want to see who rules the Arena right now you can check the
      Leaderboard.
  - Name: tut_10_9
    Text: At the end of each week, your reward will arrive by mail-based on your
      rank.
  - Name: tut_10_10
    Text: So get in there, Scion.Let them know exactly who you are.
  - Name: next
    Text: Next
  - Name: skip_this_tutorial
    Text: Do you want to skip this tutorial
  - Name: skip_this_tutorial1
    Text: Do you want to skip this tutorial
  - Name: watch_ads_to_claim
    Text: Do you want to claim double reward ?
  - Name: double_reward
    Text: x2 Reward
  - Name: arena_mess_reset
    Text: Do you wish to spend 10 Gems to refresh your Arena opponents?
  - Name: mail_reward_title
    Text: Mail Rewards
  - Name: title_wc_mail
    Text: 'Welcome to Myrk: Echoes of the Forgotten'
  - Name: detail_wc_mail
    Text: "To the Newly Awakened Scion, \r\nThe stars have aligned, and your journey
      begins.\r\nWelcome to Myrk: Echoes of the Forgotten - a world of elemental
      power, ancient prophecy, and untold adventure. We are honored to have you join
      our growing fellowship of Scion warriors.\r\nAs a token of our gratitude, a
      Welcome Package has been placed in your inventory. Inside, you'll find exclusive
      items to aid you in your training and prepare you for the challenges that lie
      ahead.\r\nShould you ever find yourself in need of guidance, our support team
      stands ready. You can reach out anytime through the in-game Help Center or
      by visiting <color=green><link=https://penguinpixelworks.com>our support team</link></color>.\r\nYour
      legend begins now. Discover hidden truths, awaken lost powers, and carve your
      name into the echoes of history.\r\nFor Gaia. For Balance. For Glory. \r\n-The
      Myrk Team-"
  - Name: title_portal_mail
    Text: Astral Gate Conquered!
  - Name: detail_portal_mail
    Text: "<b>Dear Esteemed Scion,</b>\r\nThe Vraekir#{0} has fallen, and the Astral
      Gate has been sealed. Thanks to your efforts, your strength has safeguarded
      our world from the chaos beyond.\r\nAs a token of gratitude, please accept
      these rewards for your bravery and contribution.\r\nContinue to rise, for greater
      challenges await beyond each Astral Gate\u2026"
  - Name: text_mail_delete_all
    Text: Delete All Mail
  - Name: text_mail_delete_all_content
    Text: Are you sure you want to delete all mail?
  - Name: arena_reward_title
    Text: Arena - Spoils of Valor
  - Name: arena_reward_detail
    Text: Champion, the clash of steel and the roar of battle within the Arena have
      been etched into the chronicles of war.  By your rank and valor, the gods of
      combat bestow upon you these rewards.  May their power forge your path your
      path toward even greater glory!
  - Name: arena_title
    Text: Arena
  - Name: crystal_gate_event_title
    Text: <sprite name=icon_snowflake>Crystal Gate<sprite name=icon_snowflake>
  - Name: crystal_gate_event_detail
    Text: "<b>Something ancient stirs beneath Gaia's frost...</b>Centuries ago, the
      largest Astral Gate was shattered to seal away the Dark Element. \r\nIts shards,
      scattered across Gaia, have long been buried, forgotten\u2026 and lost to myth.\r\nBut
      whispers are spreading far and wide of crystal fragments <sprite name=gate_crystal>
      being found once more.\r\nCalling to be found by Scions far and wide.\r\nThe
      world prepares - for what, none can say.\r\n<sprite name=icon_snowflake> The
      Crystal Gate Event begins soon.<b>December {0} - January {1}</b>"
  - Name: btn_remove_ads
    Text: Remove ADS
  - Name: title_remove_ads
    Text: Remove ADS
  - Name: des_remove_ads
    Text: Unlock an uninterrupted adventure! Remove all ads to enjoy smoother battles,
      faster progression, and an immersive journey without distractions.
  - Name: battle_1_1_1
    Text: By the Elements... you are awake! Stars above, I never believed I would
      see this day!  To be able to stand in the presence of a Scion, a being of prophecy!
  - Name: battle_1_1_2
    Text: "I am Soryn, a descendant of the Sentinels who once served the Astral Alliance
      before the Great Collapse shattered everything. The Alliance is dust now, forgotten
      by most. But I was never able to let go. Call it obsession if you like\u2026
      something deeper drove me.  A whisper in my blood, guiding me to find you.
      And now, with a new threat rising beyond the outer rim of the galaxy, I fear
      Gaia won't survive without you."
  - Name: battle_1_1_3
    Text: "Through my research, I uncovered writings about the prophet Myrk.  It
      gave me visions of a hidden temple, buried deep beneath the world, left untouched
      since the severing. If the legends are true, it may hold the last hope of protecting
      Gaia. But first\u2026 we must leave these ruins. The path ahead is broken,
      and not all of Aeterna's ghosts are content to sleep."
  - Name: battle_1_5_1
    Text: "It was a tragedy\u2026 what happened after the Great Collapse. The severing
      of Gaia from the stars wasn't an act of abandonment.  It was a sacrifice. Those
      who remained made an impossible choice: to sever the cosmic tether in order
      to stop the Void's advance. And it worked\u2026 for a time."
  - Name: battle_1_5_2
    Text: But the cost was heavy. Entire worlds dimmed. The Astral Alliance fractured.
      And here on Gaia, the elements; once revered and woven into daily life now
      became symbols of fear. Their use was outlawed across the galaxy, buried beneath
      edicts and silence. They feared the Void would hear them again... and come
      calling.
  - Name: battle_1_5_3
    Text: That's enough history for now. Let's hurry out of these ruins as they are
      too much of a reminder of what has been lost.
  - Name: battle_1_10_1
    Text: "I've read the old records from before the Collapse, Aeterna was more than
      just stone and silence. It was a beacon. Scholars from across the galaxy came
      here to master elemental arts, and many of the greatest Sentinels were trained
      within these halls. One of them\u2026 may have been my great, great, great
      grandmother. She was off-world when Gaia severed itself. Otherwise\u2026 I
      may never have been born."
  - Name: battle_1_10_2
    Text: "Strange to walk through the ashes of a place once so alive. But we're
      nearly through. One last battle stands between us and the open wilds. This
      one feels different\u2026. stronger, darker. I hope you're ready, Scion. Gaia
      is watching."
  - Name: battle_2_1_1
    Text: "Did you see that? The roots\u2026 they moved. On their own. This place
      has to be haunted."
  - Name: battle_2_1_2
    Text: According to one of Myrk's old texts, Whisperwood was once a sanctuary.
      A sacred grove where Druids communed with elemental spirits and the world itself
      was alive in harmony. But now? It's all twisted. The trees groan, the mists
      don't burn away, and I swear the moss watches us when we sleep.
  - Name: battle_2_1_3
    Text: "I don't like it. Let's get through here quickly. This forest remembers
      things\u2026 and not all of them are kind."
  - Name: battle_2_5_1
    Text: Since the Collapse, when the elemental gates were sealed and the Void finally
      dispersed, the remnants of the Astral Alliance fell apart. Without the elements,
      the great civilizations had no power to hold them together. Most drifted into
      silence and scattered to the stars.
  - Name: battle_2_5_2
    Text: "But some\u2026 refused to let go. A handful of Sentinels; with my ancestors
      among them, went into hiding. They kept the old ways alive, secretly practicing
      the elemental crafts in forgotten corners of the galaxy, hoping to preserve
      knowledge that others feared. But even that became dangerous."
  - Name: battle_2_5_3
    Text: "Over the centuries, fear turned to hatred. Sentinels were hunted down,
      blamed for the Collapse, accused of inviting the Void's return. By the time
      I was born, our kind had nearly vanished. Only whispers remained. And yet\u2026
      here we are. Maybe the elements haven't abandoned us after all."
  - Name: battle_2_10_1
    Text: "You hear that? Low\u2026 guttural. Almost like the trees are breathing."
  - Name: battle_2_10_2
    Text: "I've read rumors about the things that dwell here. Old warnings passed
      down in Sentinel scrolls. One creature in particular\u2026 they called it the
      Thornmaw. A beast twisted by elemental corruption. Bark as armor, thorns like
      spears, and a hunger for anything that breathes. No one's ever brought back
      a clear recording before. Just clawed-up journals and broken relics."
  - Name: battle_2_10_3
    Text: Whatever's waiting ahead, it won't let us leave without a fight. Stay sharp,
      Scion. This forest may have been a sanctuary once, but now it feels more like
      a trial.
  - Name: battle_3_1_1
    Text: "Do you hear that? The echoes\u2026 they don't sound natural. It's like
      the past itself is whispering through the stone. These caves hold more than
      silence."
  - Name: battle_3_1_2
    Text: "The word \u2018echo' makes me think of the elements. Once vibrant, living
      forces and now reduced to remnants, shadows of what they were. But you, Scion
      of Gaia\u2026 you're different. Even after centuries of sleep, your bond with
      the elements hasn't faded."
  - Name: battle_3_1_3
    Text: "They still answer your call. These beasts of flame, wind, and stone rally
      to your side. It gives me hope. If echoes of the past still carry power\u2026
      maybe the future isn't lost."
  - Name: battle_3_5_1
    Text: "Did you see that? For a moment\u2026 I swear I saw them. Scions. Echoes.
      Elemental forces surging like waves through the dark. They were locked in battle
      against monstrous voidborn creatures. It wasn't just sound bouncing off stone.
      It was a vision\u2026 a memory."
  - Name: battle_3_5_2
    Text: For you, it must feel familiar. A past life rising to the surface. You
      were there, weren't you? Not just a witness but a warrior. You fought in those
      ancient battles, didn't you?
  - Name: battle_3_5_3
    Text: "I only know the stories as fragments passed down from sentinels who barely
      understood what came before. But seeing it with my own eyes, even for a moment\u2026
      It's like watching history breathe. These caves aren't empty. They remember."
  - Name: battle_3_10_1
    Text: In one of the prophet Myrk's oldest scrolls, there's a passage, though
      barely legible, about a sacred temple buried far beneath Gaia. Most dismissed
      it as metaphor, or the ramblings of a mystic. But these caves... They match
      the descriptions. The layout, the elemental signatures... it's possible the
      Temple of Myrk is real, and we may be getting closer.
  - Name: battle_3_10_2
    Text: But first, we have to make it through whatever's guarding this final chamber.
      I can feel it, the pressure, the silence before the storm. This battle will
      be unlike the ones before. If we survive it, the Scion's Path awaits.
  - Name: battle_4_1_1
    Text: I've read that this mountain pass was once a proving ground. Those seeking
      to become Scions walked it alone, facing trials designed to test not just strength,
      but wisdom and will. Few completed it. Fewer survived unchanged.
  - Name: battle_4_1_2
    Text: "Now it's your turn although you're no student, not anymore. The path hasn't
      forgotten what it demands. Let's see how far your bond with the elemental echoes
      has come. This journey will shape more than the world\u2026 it will shape you."
  - Name: battle_4_5_1
    Text: I've always wondered what the Scions felt when they walked this path. Some
      say the winds would turn sharp, the storms cruel, as if Gaia herself challenged
      their resolve. Records speak of Scions driven mad, broken by illusions, or
      even turned back by the weight of their own fears. This path doesn't just test
      your strength; it breaks open your soul.
  - Name: battle_4_5_2
    Text: "During my search for Gaia, I stumbled upon an old vault buried deep on
      a derelict moon. Inside, I found a star map etched with coordinates long erased
      from known charts as well as a sigil I'd only seen once before, in a prophecy
      tied to Myrk. It described a temple far older than the Collapse, even older
      even than the Alliance itself. I think we're on the path to something ancient\u2026
      and sacred."
  - Name: battle_4_10_1
    Text: "Not long before I rediscovered Gaia, I started hearing whispers \u2014
      rumors of the Dark Void returning. Worlds on the outer edges of the galaxy
      were going dark, vanishing from the astral beacons one by one. But this time,
      it isn't just the elemental chaos... survivors speak of forms. Shapes. As if
      the Void has begun to wear a face."
  - Name: battle_4_10_2
    Text: We can speak more of this once we reach Cindergate. There's more you must
      know. But for now, the last of this path awaits us. And I fear what lies ahead
      may test us more than anything we've faced so far.
  - Name: battle_5_1_1
    Text: 'This town won''t welcome us. Whatever machines still function here will
      see us as intruders, not allies. Long ago, Cindergate was a marvel. It was
      the heart of all things mechanical. Bots once roamed these streets with purpose:
      greeting travelers, fixing ships, even aiding Sentinels with their elemental
      studies.'
  - Name: battle_5_1_2
    Text: "But when the Great Collapse struck, something changed. Stories tell of
      memory wipes gone wrong, of machines turning against their creators in confusion
      and violence. What couldn't be shut down was abandoned\u2026 left to decay
      and defend a town that no longer remembers why it was built."
  - Name: battle_5_5_1
    Text: "I think I found something in the remains of our last battle. It looks
      like a memory core. Surprisingly intact. It's encrypted, but I managed to access
      fragments. It's strange\u2026 almost like it was intended for a Scion. There's
      a map encoded within that leads through a swamp, then a vast desert, and eventually
      around what looks like a volcano. This might be the path we've been searching
      for\u2026 and if there's more memory cores like this, we're likely to find
      more answers along the way."
  - Name: battle_5_5_2
    Text: There was more. The core held logs from the final days of Cindergate. After
      the Collapse, the town's central processor was a construct known as Axiom and
      it issued a defensive purge protocol. Their prime directive became survival
      and perimeter control. Without purpose, without people, they turned on everything
      and even each other. This town didn't just fall. It tore itself apart.
  - Name: battle_5_10_1
    Text: "You remember when I spoke of the Void returning? Well\u2026 I've heard
      whispers across the outer sectors. They say the Void now has a face. The Vraekir,
      those insectoid scavengers who once lurked in junkyards and clung to the edges
      of civilization, now they've changed. Some say they merged with the Void\u2026
      or were devoured by it. Either way, they're no longer the desperate creatures
      we once pitied. They're something else now, something dangerous."
  - Name: battle_5_10_2
    Text: "If their hunger still drives them, they'll seek Gaia, especially if they
      sense your awakening. We must grow stronger, faster. You were not just awakened
      to reclaim the past, Scion\u2026 you were awakened to defend the future."
  - Name: battle_6_1_1
    Text: "There is no way this place was once a fertile basin\u2026 The stench alone
      is enough to strip paint from steel! It's as if every dying thing in Gaia came
      here to rot and to be swallowed by the bog and forgotten. If the creatures
      don't get us, the fumes surely will."
  - Name: battle_6_1_2
    Text: "Tread carefully, Scion. The ground shifts with our every step, like it's
      watching\u2026 waiting. This swamp doesn't welcome us. It breathes, it listens,
      and it remembers. I fear it knows who you are."
  - Name: battle_6_5_1
    Text: Do you feel that? The elements here... they twist and churn like something
      is poisoning them. This isn't natural. It's as if the Void left a wound here,
      and the swamp never healed. Even the elemental creatures that respond to your
      call seem hesitant, like they're wading through a fog of corruption. Something
      is wrong beneath the surface.
  - Name: battle_6_5_2
    Text: "There are whispers too, not just the kind that rustle through reeds. These
      are voices. Old ones. Spirits perhaps, tethered to the muck and mire since
      the Great Collapse. I can't tell if they're warning us\u2026 or luring us deeper.
      Either way, I don't trust the dead when they don't stay dead."
  - Name: battle_6_10_1
    Text: Earlier, I stumbled across what looked like temple stones. They were submerged
      and cracked, half-eaten by vines and moss. Symbols that resemble the old Sentinels'
      crest. It's possible that a sanctuary once stood here, long forgotten. If that's
      true, this swamp may be more than just a graveyard. It is so sad just to think
      of what things once were.
  - Name: battle_6_10_2
    Text: I think we're about out of here. It seems things are starting to dry up
      fast and get much hotter. This last battle might finally bring some fresh air
      to our lungs, and that's not saying things lightly.
  - Name: battle_7_1_1
    Text: "Out of the skillet into the frying pan. It was a sauna, but now it's just
      hot. This place was once known as the Sea of Solvenar. A golden body of water
      flowing through lands of shimmering beauty and astral resonance. But after
      Gaia was sealed off from the stars, the ley lines fractured. The water dried,
      the sand crept in, and what life remained beneath it\u2026 withered. Now, they
      call it Gaia's Grief, not in anger, but in mourning."
  - Name: battle_7_1_2
    Text: If we can make it to the halfway point, I've heard there are ruins we might
      shelter in. With any luck, they'll hold a clue as to what or where we need
      to go next. Just keep your eyes sharp. Things don't stay buried here for long,
      especially not the past.
  - Name: battle_7_5_1
    Text: "Well, we were lucky enough to find some shelter in these ruins. I think
      that last battle knocked over some walls and behind one of them\u2026 something
      strange. An old parchment, brittle and scorched, showing what this land used
      to be before it all dried up. Verdant trails, flowing ley lines, and in the
      center\u2026 a great red circle. According to this, if we keep going the direction
      we've been headed, then turn right at the ridge, we'll be walking straight
      into it."
  - Name: battle_7_5_2
    Text: Sometimes, I wonder if the prophet Myrk is guiding our every step. His
      teachings spoke often of elemental flows and unseen paths. I've always had
      a bit of faith in his words. If his spirit is with us now, then perhaps he's
      leading us to exactly what we need to stand against the darkness that's coming.
  - Name: battle_7_10_1
    Text: We're almost out of this heat. I hope the next stretch of our journey is
      much cooler. I should've studied more about the Water Element and maybe I could've
      pulled a drop or two from these dry bones to cool myself down. Though I don't
      see you sweating, Scion. You always did have that otherworldly composure.
  - Name: battle_7_10_2
    Text: Prepare yourself. The sands are shifting... and something's moving beneath
      us. I just hope it's not one of those Rustipedes. Nasty things, giant, metal-shelled
      centipedes that burrow through stone and steel alike. They don't discriminate.
      If it breathes or shines, they devour it. Let's finish this fight, and move
      on. No need to wait for whatever it is to come to us.
  - Name: battle_8_1_1
    Text: By the Elements, we can never catch a break. It just keeps getting hotter
      and hotter. I would assume that this is the Ring of Ashenfall. I read that
      this was once a sacred path... a pilgrimage route for Scions to study the Element
      of Fire. Trials of endurance, mastery, and control that is forged in the heat
      of molten stone. Now, I just hope those same fire elements stay buried deep
      within the volcano's heart.
  - Name: battle_8_1_2
    Text: In the distance, I can see the broken spires of temple ruins. If we're
      lucky, they may hold records or symbols tied to the Astral Alliance, or maybe
      even Myrk himself. We've followed a trail of secrets across half of Gaia, and
      if these ruins echo anything of their former glory, they might help us find
      what lies ahead.
  - Name: battle_8_1_3
    Text: "I haven't told you everything about how I found Gaia. My ancestors were
      Sentinels, yes, but my life was spent chasing myths. Whispers in derelict spaceports.
      Star maps scribbled in forgotten journals. They all pointed here to this lost
      world, sealed from the cosmos. Most laughed at me. But when I first saw the
      broken Gate signature within this star system\u2026 I knew. Something ancient
      still pulsed here. And now you're awake, Scion. It wasn't madness. It was destiny."
  - Name: battle_8_5_1
    Text: I don't think we'll find much here. Everything seems to be sifted through
      quite well over the years. Looters, scavengers, even time itself, and they've
      all had their turn stripping this temple of meaning. We'd have to be quite
      lucky to find anything at all.
  - Name: battle_8_5_2
    Text: "But just as Soryn turns to leave, a loose stone slab beneath his foot
      shifts with a hollow clunk. He kneels, brushing away centuries of dust, revealing
      a faint glyph scorched into the floor; a spiral of flame surrounding a gate
      symbol. \u201CBy the stars... this wasn't on any of the old temple schematics
      I studied.\u201D Pressing the glyph causes a section of the wall to groan and
      shift, revealing a scorched relief: a mural showing Scions descending a hidden
      path into the base of the volcano, flames parting before them as if the mountain
      itself recognized their presence."
  - Name: battle_8_5_3
    Text: There at the volcano's base. That's no ordinary lava tube. It's a sealed
      path, one only Scions could open. Looks like our next trial lies beneath the
      fire, not around it. Ready yourself, Scion. The real test begins now.
  - Name: battle_8_10_1
    Text: I think this is where we need to be, but I don't see anything," Soryn mutters,
      scanning the jagged obsidian ridges at the volcano's base. Ash swirls in the
      heated air, and the ground pulses with faint, rhythmic tremors, like a heartbeat
      deep within the mountain. Just then, you step forward. The sigils on their
      gauntlet begin to glow faintly, responding to an unseen call.
  - Name: battle_8_10_2
    Text: The ground begins to shimmer, not from heat but from power. A ring of ancient
      runes, long buried beneath dust and soot, ignites in a vibrant blaze. Fire
      and stone twist and part, revealing a staircase sewn from blackened basalt
      that spirals downward into the mountain's heart. The very mountain groans,
      not in protest, but as if recognizing an heir returning home.
  - Name: battle_8_10_3
    Text: The fire elementals are upon us! We must defeat these creatures in order
      to proceed onward. Scion, this is your battle! Show them that you are the Scion
      of prophecy and that you have returned!
  - Name: battle_9_1_1
    Text: It looks like these steps go down forever. I don't see the end. Just more
      steps and darkness. At least every so often there is a platform, so we may
      rest.
  - Name: battle_9_1_2
    Text: "The ancient walls pulse faintly with soft ethereal light. Etched murals
      shift and shimmer, depicting long-lost Scions walking this very path. Its wielders
      of elemental might are locked in struggle and glory. Some faces are clear,
      proud and victorious. Others are blurred, perhaps forgotten\u2026 or erased.
      Illusions whisper wordless echoes, drawing the Scion into glimpses of triumphs
      now buried by time."
  - Name: battle_9_1_3
    Text: But respite is a luxury not granted for long. As you step onto the first
      resting platform, the shadows stir. Manifestations of ancient trials, creatures
      shaped by the temple's will, surge forth, drawn to test the strength of any
      who dare descend. Soryn draws his weapon with urgency.
  - Name: battle_9_1_4
    Text: The Temple watches us, Scion. We must prove ourselves worthy.
  - Name: battle_9_5_1
    Text: "Finally, some relief from the heat. I believe we're far enough from the
      volcano now. Though\u2026 with how long we've been descending, this way, that
      way, in spirals and in silence. We could be anywhere beneath Gaia by now. Myrk
      hid this path well. I can only wonder what lies at the end of these stairs."
  - Name: battle_9_5_2
    Text: "The Prophet Myrk rarely wrote plainly, but in one fragment I found, he
      spoke of 'a vault far beneath Gaia's skin, where silence holds the key and
      prophecy meets its destiny.' I believe he meant this place. This descent isn't
      just a path, but a rite. The closer we get to the temple, the more I feel like
      we're stepping not just through space\u2026 but through time itself. Your awakening,
      Scion, may be the final piece to a prophecy centuries in the making."
  - Name: battle_9_10_1
    Text: The shadows begin to thin as the stairs give way to a vast, ancient chamber,
      its ceiling lost in darkness. A faint rumble stirs beneath their feet as the
      stone floor begins to rotate, intricate rings shifting to reveal a new challenge.
      From the circling stone emerge twisted guardians, ancient creatures bound to
      defend whatever lies beyond.
  - Name: battle_9_10_2
    Text: It seems we've reached the end of this long journey downward... But of
      course, there's one final test. One more battle between us and the truth that
      waits in the deep." Soryn pauses, then smiles with a spark of pride.
  - Name: battle_9_10_3
    Text: "This place\u2026 this journey... it deserves a name. \"Descent of the
      Scion. Yes. I like the sound of that. Let all who walk these steps after us
      know that the Scion has returned, and carved a path into legend."
  - Name: battle_10_1_1
    Text: As the duo steps into the heart of the cavern, their eyes widen. A vast
      subterranean expanse stretches before them, large enough to house an entire
      village, with glowing crystals embedded in the cavern ceiling casting an ethereal
      light across ancient stonework.
  - Name: battle_10_1_2
    Text: This place is enormous! How did Myrk keep this place hidden for so many
      centuries?
  - Name: battle_10_1_3
    Text: "The one named Myrk\u2026 he was no mere mortal. He foresaw everything,
      every rise and fall, every fracture and silence. A thousand years of fate,
      all winding down to this moment."
  - Name: battle_10_1_4
    Text: "As you follow a smooth, winding path toward the temple at the center,
      murals line the stone walls, faded, yet vividly alive. They depict scenes from
      history\u2026 wars, awakenings, elemental ascension."
  - Name: battle_10_1_5
    Text: "Soryn stops abruptly, placing a hand on one particular wall. \"Look at
      this painting! It's me\u2026 waking you in the Ruins of Aeterna. This place...
      it must be laced with prophecy. Or magic beyond our understanding. Myrk planned
      all of this. And we're just now catching up."
  - Name: battle_10_5_1
    Text: These walls..." Soryn murmurs, his fingers brushing over another shifting
      mural, "they depict our whole journey here. From the Ruins to the Forest, through
      fire and sand. I wonder when we reach the center, will they show us what comes
      next?
  - Name: battle_10_5_2
    Text: "Soryn pauses, eyes narrowing at the radiant glow far ahead. \"It's still
      a ways off, but that light\u2026 It's no ordinary flame. I think we're halfway
      there. And whatever awaits us might be the only thing strong enough to stop
      the Vraekir before they reach Gaia."
  - Name: battle_10_5_3
    Text: As you press forward through the temple's corridors, the air hums with
      quiet energy. Hallways shift gently under your steps as if the entire structure
      is alive, responding to your presence. Floating glyphs light the path, flickering
      with elemental colors long thought forgotten. Statues of past Scions line the
      walls, some familiar from murals, others completely unknown, each holding relics
      of power and prophecy. The sense of destiny grows heavier with every step toward
      the temple's radiant heart.
  - Name: battle_10_10_1
    Text: "This is it! Our final battle\u2026 Scion, I know it has been a long journey,
      but I have believed in you from the very start. Past these creatures is what
      we've come for. The key to Gaia's future. The prophecy ends, or begins here."
  - Name: battle_10_10_2
    Text: "Soryn, places a hand on your shoulder, eyes steady and unwavering. \u201CWe've
      crossed the Ruins of Aeterna, wandered through the haunted wilds of Whisperwood,
      unraveled ancient machines in Cindergate, and braved the stench and spirits
      of Gravemire. We crossed Gaia's Grief, climbed the Ring of Ashenfall, and descended
      deeper than anyone since the Collapse. You've proven your strength in every
      test. This final trial is not just a battle, but the culmination of everything
      the galaxy has waited for. Now\u2026 let's finish what Myrk began."
  - Name: crystal_gate_event_title
    Text: "Centuries ago, during the final days of the Astral Alliance, the largest
      and only Astral Gate on Gaia was destroyed to prevent the Dark Element from
      consuming the planet\u2019s elemental core. When the gate shattered, its crystal
      fragments rained across Gaia./nFor generations, these shards - now known as
      Gate Crystals - were sealed within treasure chests or left untouched, believed
      to be cursed remnants of the Collapse. But as the year turns and Gaia\u2019s
      light renews, the crystals have begun to resonate once more, humming faintly
      with restored energy. Merchants across the world now seek these relics, offering
      rare treasures in exchange for any Scion that happens to recover them."
  - Name: crystal_gate_event_summary
    Text: "During the Christmas and New Year\u2019s season, players can collect Gate
      Crystal Pieces,  remnants of Gaia\u2019s shattered Astral Gate, and exchange
      them for valuable prizes through the event merchants."
--- !u!1 &1331513142
